* Week 9: {{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1993-09-25.pdf|title=Top 10 Sales in Europe|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=10|issue=39|date=25 September 1993|page=22|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240307015834/https://worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1993-09-25.pdf|archive-date=7 March 2024|access-date=31 March 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> Spain (2 weeks),<ref name="spain">"All That She Wants" spent 2 weeks at number one on the Spanish singles chart in May and August 1993.
* Week 1: {{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1993-05-29.pdf|title=Top 10 Sales in Europe|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=10|issue=22|date=29 May 1993|page=34|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240307015635/https://worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1993-05-29.pdf|archive-date=7 March 2024|access-date=31 March 2024|url-status=live}}
* Week 2: {{cite magazine|url=https://www.worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1993-08-07.pdf|title=Top 10 Sales in Europe|magazine=[[Music & Media]]|volume=10|issue=|date=7 August 1993|page=16|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251125005818/https://worldradiohistory.com/UK/Music-and-Media/90s/1993/MM-1993-08-07.pdf|archive-date=25 November 2025|access-date=31 March 2024|url-status=live}}</ref> Switzerland (2 weeks),<ref name="switzerland"/> and the United Kingdom. In the latter, it peaked in its third week at the [[UK Singles Chart]], on 16 May 1993.<ref name="UK"/> It spent three weeks at the top position on the chart after debuting as number five. The song peaked at top three positions in most other places where it was released. "All That She Wants" peaked at number two on the [[Eurochart Hot 100]] in June,<ref name="eurocharthot100">{{cite magazine|title= Hits of the World |magazine= [[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |date= 12 June 1993 |volume= 105 |issue= 24 |page= 57 |issn= 0006-2510 |url= https://books.google.com/books?id=9A8EAAAAMBAJ&q=%22all+that+she+wants+ace+of+base%22&pg=PA59-IA14}}</ref> being held off the top position by [[Snow (musician)|Snow]]'s "[[Informer (song)|Informer]]". The song was a very successful radio hit in the United States, peaking at number one on the US ''Billboard'' [[Mainstream Top 40|Top 40 Mainstream]] chart.<ref name="Pop"/> On the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] and [[Cash Box Top 100 Pop Singles|''Cash Box'' Top 100]], it peaked at number two and three.<ref name="Hot 100"/><ref name="cashbox">{{cite magazine|title= Cash Box Top 100 Pop Singles – Week ending November 27, 1993 |magazine= [[Cashbox (magazine)|Cash Box]] |url= http://cashboxmagazine.com/archives/90s_files/19931127.html |archive-date= 10 October 2012 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20121010155216/http://cashboxmagazine.com/archives/90s_files/19931127.html}}</ref> On the Canadian ''[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]'' Dance/Urban chart, it peaked at number one for 4 weeks.<ref>"All That She Wants" spent 4 weeks at number one on the Canadian ''[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]'' Dance/Urban chart in November 1993.
* Week 1: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=6714&app=rpm|title=RPM Dance|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=58|issue=17|date=6 November 1993|page=}}
* Week 2: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=6715&app=rpm|title=RPM Dance|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=58|issue=18|date=13 November 1993|page=}}
* Week 3: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=6724&app=rpm|title=RPM Dance|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=58|issue=19|date=20 November 1993|page=}}
* Week 4: {{cite magazine|url=https://recherche-collection-search.bac-lac.gc.ca/eng/home/record?IdNumber=1496&app=rpm|title=RPM Dance|magazine=[[RPM (magazine)|RPM]]|volume=58|issue=20|date=27 November 1993|page=}}</ref>

"All That She Wants" was listed at number nine on the ''Billboard'' 1994 year-end charts and at number 70 on the 1990s decade-end charts. In Germany, the song was the best-selling single of 1993.<ref name="Germany"/> It sold 604,000 copies in the United Kingdom in 1993.<ref>{{cite web |first= Rob |last= Copsey |title= Official Top 40 best-selling songs of 1993 |publisher= [[Official Charts Company]] |date= 4 June 2021 |accessdate= 10 July 2021 |url= https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/official-top-40-best-selling-songs-of-1993__33290/ |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20220201043453/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/official-top-40-best-selling-songs-of-1993__33290/ |archive-date= 1 February 2022 |url-status= live}}</ref> According to [[Edel-Mega Records|Mega Records]], the single sold 3.7 million copies worldwide as of May 1998.<ref name="wwsales">{{cite magazine|first1= Charles |last1= Ferro |first2= Kai R. |last2= Lofthus |title= Ace of Base Sprouts 'Flowers' |magazine= Billboard |date= 30 May 1998 |volume= 110 |issue= 22 |pages= 70, 85 |issn= 0006-2510 |url= https://books.google.com/books?id=fQ4EAAAAMBAJ&pg=PA70}}</ref>

